  "answer": "## What to change\n\nAdd a new boolean prop to `Badge` (e.g. `disabled`) that suppresses rendering of the badge element so no badge background/color is shown—matching the behavior you described.\n\nThe badge markup is currently rendered unconditionally in `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/Badge.js`, around the area you referenced (`Badge.js#L68` in v1-beta.34).\n\n## Mechanism (where to implement)\n\n1. **Extend the `Badge` component API**\n   - In `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/Badge.js`, update the component’s props handling to accept `disabled` (default `false`).\n   - If `disabled` is `true`, return only the child (e.g. your `<Avatar />`) and do not render the badge `<span class=\"MuiBadge-badge\" ...>`.\n\n2. **Update styling/logic**\n   - The key is to **not render the badge span at all**, rather than rendering it with `display: none` (which still may leave layout/background artifacts depending on styles and wrappers).\n\n3. **Update TypeScript types / entry exports**\n   - `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/index.d.ts` exists and should be updated to include the new `disabled?: boolean` prop (this repo references that file as a consumer of `Badge.js`).\n   - Keep `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/index.js` as-is (it just re-exports `Badge`).\n\n## Files involved\n\n- **Implement behavior:** `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/Badge.js` (logic around the badge rendering near the cited `#L68`)\n- **Add prop to TS types:** `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/index.d.ts` (currently imported/maintained as part of the Badge public API)\n- **(Optional) Tests:** `packages/material-ui/src/Badge/Badge.test.js` to cover `disabled={true}` rendering only children.\n\nIf you’d like, paste the current `Badge.js` source body excerpt around the badge render section and I can suggest an exact patch (diff-style).",
